dho:p-mn10-36.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-mn10-36.2 ;
    skos:note "Sense of dhamma here is contested; deliberately left unassigned in v0.1."@en ;
    dho:inText dho:t-mn10 ;
    dho:segment "mn10:36.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of principles with respect to the five hindrances."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu dhammesu dhammānupassī viharati pañcasu nīvaraṇesu."@pi ;
    dho:translatorRendering "principles (Sujato)" ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn10/en/sujato#mn10:36.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:sim-body-food-factors a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-body-food-factors ;
    skos:prefLabel "the body sustained by food (the awakening factors)"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.2-16.1,
        dho:p-sn46.2-16.2,
        dho:p-sn46.2-8.1,
        dho:p-sn46.2-8.2 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:n-06,
        dho:n-07,
        dho:n-08,
        dho:n-09,
        dho:n-10,
        dho:n-11,
        dho:n-12 ;
    dho:image "This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue." .

dho:sim-body-food-hindrances a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-body-food-hindrances ;
    skos:prefLabel "the body sustained by food (the hindrances)"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.2-1.2,
        dho:p-sn46.2-1.3,
        dho:p-sn46.2-7.1,
        dho:p-sn46.2-7.2 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:n-01,
        dho:n-02,
        dho:n-03,
        dho:n-04,
        dho:n-05 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, this body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, the five hindrances are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue." .

dho:sim-bowl-boiling a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-bowl-boiling ;
    skos:prefLabel "a bowl of water heated and boiling"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.55-6.1,
        dho:p-sn46.55-6.2,
        dho:p-sn46.55-6.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-g2 ;
    dho:image "Suppose there was a bowl of water that was heated by fire, boiling and bubbling." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed." .

dho:sim-bowl-dyed a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-bowl-dyed ;
    skos:prefLabel "a bowl of water mixed with dye"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.55-4.1,
        dho:p-sn46.55-4.2,
        dho:p-sn46.55-4.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-g1 ;
    dho:image "Suppose there was a bowl of water that was mixed with dye such as red lac, turmeric, indigo, or rose madder." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed." .

dho:sim-bowl-moss a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-bowl-moss ;
    skos:prefLabel "a bowl of water covered with moss"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.55-8.1,
        dho:p-sn46.55-8.2,
        dho:p-sn46.55-8.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-g3 ;
    dho:image "Suppose there was a bowl of water enveloped with moss and aquatic plants." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed." .

dho:sim-bowl-muddy a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-bowl-muddy ;
    skos:prefLabel "a bowl of muddy water in the dark"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.55-12.1,
        dho:p-sn46.55-12.2,
        dho:p-sn46.55-12.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-g5 ;
    dho:image "Suppose there was a bowl of water that was cloudy, murky, and muddy, hidden in the darkness." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, there’s a time when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt and you don’t truly understand the escape from doubt that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both. Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed." .

dho:sim-bowl-wind a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-bowl-wind ;
    skos:prefLabel "a bowl of water stirred by the wind"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.55-10.1,
        dho:p-sn46.55-10.2,
        dho:p-sn46.55-10.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-g4 ;
    dho:image "Suppose there was a bowl of water stirred by the wind, quivering, swirling, and rippling." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed." .

dho:sim-dawn-attention a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-dawn-attention ;
    skos:note "The same image as for good friendship (SN 46.12), with a different point, so a separate simile."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "the dawn before the sunrise (rational application of mind)"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.13-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.13-1.2 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-04 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors." .

dho:sim-dawn-friendship a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-dawn-friendship ;
    skos:note "The same simile, with the same point, in SN 46.12 and 46.48 (D12)."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "the dawn before the sunrise (good friendship)"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.12-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.12-1.2,
        dho:p-sn46.48-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.48-1.2 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-02 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors." .

dho:sim-dragons a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-dragons ;
    skos:note "The dragons grow strong on the mountain, then go down to pools, lakes, streams, rivers and the ocean, acquiring a great and abundant body (1.3); so the mendicant, grounded on ethics, acquires great and abundant good qualities."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "dragons growing strong on the Himalayas"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.1-1.2,
        dho:p-sn46.1-1.3,
        dho:p-sn46.1-1.4 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-01 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, dragons grow and wax strong supported by the Himalayas, the king of mountains." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities." .

dho:sim-earth a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-earth ;
    skos:prefLabel "living creatures depending on the earth"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.11-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.11-1.2,
        dho:p-sn46.11-1.3 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-01 ;
    dho:image "sometimes walking, sometimes standing, sometimes sitting, sometimes lying down—all do so depending on the earth and grounded on the earth." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics." .

dho:sim-fire-great-dry a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-fire-great-dry ;
    skos:note "Trying to put out a great fire with dry fuel and blowing on it: the restless mind and the wrong factors."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "dry fuel on a great fire"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.53-11.1,
        dho:p-sn46.53-11.2,
        dho:p-sn46.53-11.3,
        dho:p-sn46.53-12.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:ta-07,
        dho:ta-08,
        dho:ta-09 ;
    dho:image "If they toss dry grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, blow on it, and don’t scatter dirt on it," ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture." .

dho:sim-fire-great-wet a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-fire-great-wet ;
    skos:note "Putting out a great fire with wet fuel, water and dirt: the restless mind and the right factors."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "wet fuel on a great fire"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.53-14.1,
        dho:p-sn46.53-14.2,
        dho:p-sn46.53-14.3,
        dho:p-sn46.53-15.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:ta-10,
        dho:ta-11,
        dho:ta-12 ;
    dho:image "If they toss wet grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, spray it with water, and scatter dirt on it," ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity." .

dho:sim-fire-small-dry a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-fire-small-dry ;
    skos:note "Making a small fire flare up with dry fuel and blowing on it: the sluggish mind and the right factors."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "dry fuel on a small fire"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.53-8.1,
        dho:p-sn46.53-8.2,
        dho:p-sn46.53-8.3,
        dho:p-sn46.53-9.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:ta-04,
        dho:ta-05,
        dho:ta-06 ;
    dho:image "If they toss dry grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, blow on it, and don’t scatter dirt on it," ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture." .

dho:sim-fire-small-wet a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-fire-small-wet ;
    skos:note "Making a small fire flare up with wet fuel, water and dirt: the sluggish mind and the wrong factors."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "wet fuel on a small fire"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.53-5.1,
        dho:p-sn46.53-5.2,
        dho:p-sn46.53-5.3,
        dho:p-sn46.53-6.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:ta-01,
        dho:ta-02,
        dho:ta-03 ;
    dho:image "If they toss wet grass, cow-dung, and timber on it, spray it with water, and scatter dirt on it," ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, when the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity." .

dho:sim-gold a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-gold ;
    skos:note "Iron, copper, tin, lead and silver are the five corruptions of gold (1.3-1.7); the point names five corruptions of the mind (cittassa upakkilesā, 2.1), not 'hindrances'."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "the five corruptions of native gold"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.33-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.3,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.4,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.5,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.6,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.7,
        dho:p-sn46.33-1.8,
        dho:p-sn46.33-2.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:FiveCorruptionsOfMind ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, there are these five corruptions of native gold. When native gold is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant, but is brittle and not completely ready for working." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements." .

dho:sim-monarch a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-monarch ;
    skos:note "The text sets the two side by side without 'just as … in the same way' (seyyathāpi … evameva); treated as a simile because the monarch's treasures are there only to illustrate (D23). The seven treasures are named in 1.3."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "the seven treasures of a Wheel-Turning Monarch"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.42-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.42-1.3,
        dho:p-sn46.42-1.4,
        dho:p-sn46.42-2.1 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:c-u3 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, when a Wheel-Turning Monarch appears seven treasures appear." ;
    dho:wording "When a Realized One, a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha appears the seven treasures of the awakening factors appear." .

dho:sim-rafters a owl:Thing,
        dho:Simile ;
    owl:sameAs dho:sim-rafters ;
    skos:prefLabel "the rafters of a bungalow"@en ;
    dho:citedBy dho:p-sn46.7-1.1,
        dho:p-sn46.7-1.2 ;
    dho:illustrates dho:o-02 ;
    dho:image "Mendicants, the rafters of a bungalow all slant, slope, and incline to the peak." ;
    dho:wording "In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment." .

