"sometimes walking, sometimes standing, sometimes sitting, sometimes lying down—all do so depending on the earth and grounded on the earth." owl:sameAs "sometimes walking, sometimes standing, sometimes sitting, sometimes lying down—all do so depending on the earth and grounded on the earth." .

"the four kinds of mindfulness meditation are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors" owl:sameAs "the four kinds of mindfulness meditation are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors" .

"the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom" owl:sameAs "the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom" .

"the seven awakening factors have been properly implemented so that they lead to living at ease" owl:sameAs "the seven awakening factors have been properly implemented so that they lead to living at ease" .

"the three kinds of good conduct are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation" owl:sameAs "the three kinds of good conduct are developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation" .

"they can expect seven fruits and benefits" owl:sameAs "they can expect seven fruits and benefits" .

"they lead to awakening" owl:sameAs "they lead to awakening" .

"upekkhāsahagataṁ" owl:sameAs "upekkhāsahagataṁ" .

"weaken wisdom" owl:sameAs "weaken wisdom" .

"yasmiṁ samaye byāpādapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati byāpādaparetena, uppannassa ca byāpādassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" owl:sameAs "yasmiṁ samaye byāpādapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati byāpādaparetena, uppannassa ca byāpādassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" .

"yasmiṁ samaye thinamiddhapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati thinamiddhaparetena, uppannassa ca thinamiddhassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" owl:sameAs "yasmiṁ samaye thinamiddhapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati thinamiddhaparetena, uppannassa ca thinamiddhassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" .

"yasmiṁ samaye uddhaccakukkuccapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati uddhaccakukkuccaparetena, uppannassa ca uddhaccakukkuccassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" owl:sameAs "yasmiṁ samaye uddhaccakukkuccapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati uddhaccakukkuccaparetena, uppannassa ca uddhaccakukkuccassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" .

"yasmiṁ samaye vicikicchāpariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati vicikicchāparetena, uppannāya ca vicikicchāya nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" owl:sameAs "yasmiṁ samaye vicikicchāpariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati vicikicchāparetena, uppannāya ca vicikicchāya nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati" .

"your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire and you don’t truly understand the escape from sensual desire that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both." owl:sameAs "your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire and you don’t truly understand the escape from sensual desire that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both." .

"'A Realized One, a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha' (tathāgata arahant sammāsambuddha), SN 46.9 and 46.42."@en owl:sameAs "'A Realized One, a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha' (tathāgata arahant sammāsambuddha), SN 46.9 and 46.42."@en .

"'Block wisdom' (paññānirodhikā) is stronger than SN 46.37's 'weaken wisdom' (paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā, o-14); both map to 'weakens' (revisit list #4)."@en owl:sameAs "'Block wisdom' (paññānirodhikā) is stronger than SN 46.37's 'weaken wisdom' (paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā, o-14); both map to 'weakens' (revisit list #4)."@en .

"'a cause and reason for' (hetu, paccaya), SN 46.56 (D16)."@en owl:sameAs "'a cause and reason for' (hetu, paccaya), SN 46.56 (D16)."@en .

"'can expect to develop and cultivate' (pāṭikaṅkha)."@en owl:sameAs "'can expect to develop and cultivate' (pāṭikaṅkha)."@en .

"'depending on and grounded on', 'relies on' (nissāya, nissita)."@en owl:sameAs "'depending on and grounded on', 'relies on' (nissāya, nissita)."@en .

"'developed and cultivated so as to fulfill' (bhāvitā bahulīkatā paripūrenti), SN 46.6 (D20)."@en owl:sameAs "'developed and cultivated so as to fulfill' (bhāvitā bahulīkatā paripūrenti), SN 46.6 (D20)."@en .

"'not apart from' (nāññatra): the conditioned don't arise apart from the condition. A necessary condition, not a sufficient one (SN 46.9, 46.10; D23)."@en owl:sameAs "'not apart from' (nāññatra): the conditioned don't arise apart from the condition. A necessary condition, not a sufficient one (SN 46.9, 46.10; D23)."@en .

"'rooted in and meet at' (mūlaka, samosaraṇa)."@en owl:sameAs "'rooted in and meet at' (mūlaka, samosaraṇa)."@en .

"'the forerunner and harbinger of' (pubbaṅgama, pubbanimitta)."@en owl:sameAs "'the forerunner and harbinger of' (pubbaṅgama, pubbanimitta)."@en .

"'when you …, X …'; the result says what happens to the conditioned."@en owl:sameAs "'when you …, X …'; the result says what happens to the conditioned."@en .

"A compound name split into its two words: thina / middha, uddhacca / kukkucca."@en owl:sameAs "A compound name split into its two words: thina / middha, uddhacca / kukkucca."@en .

"A condition the mind is in at a given time, e.g. a sluggish mind (līnaṁ cittaṁ). Kept separate from the hindrances on purpose: see DECISIONS.md D6."@en owl:sameAs "A condition the mind is in at a given time, e.g. a sluggish mind (līnaṁ cittaṁ). Kept separate from the hindrances on purpose: see DECISIONS.md D6."@en .

"A link this project draws that no text states outright. Always shown as the editor's view."@en owl:sameAs "A link this project draws that no text states outright. Always shown as the editor's view."@en .

"A mendicant gives up bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind, and develops good conduct by way of body, speech, and mind."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant gives up bad conduct by way of body, speech, and mind, and develops good conduct by way of body, speech, and mind."@en .

"A mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of the body—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of the body—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world."@en .

"A mendicant who is diligent can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant who is diligent can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors."@en .

"A one-to-one pairing of a quality against a hindrance. The suttas give the sets; the pairing comes from the commentaries."@en owl:sameAs "A one-to-one pairing of a quality against a hindrance. The suttas give the sets; the pairing comes from the commentaries."@en .

"A quality of mind that can arise, grow, or be abandoned."@en owl:sameAs "A quality of mind that can arise, grow, or be abandoned."@en .

"A quality of mind, e.g. 'qualities that are skillful and unskillful' (kusalākusalā dhammā)."@en owl:sameAs "A quality of mind, e.g. 'qualities that are skillful and unskillful' (kusalākusalā dhammā)."@en .

"A small, citation-first ontology of the hindrances, awakening factors and jhāna factors, built from the Pali suttas. Every doctrinal link points to the passage that states it."@en owl:sameAs "A small, citation-first ontology of the hindrances, awakening factors and jhāna factors, built from the Pali suttas. Every doctrinal link points to the passage that states it."@en .

"A statement of purpose: the factors 'should be developed for' (bhāvetabbā) four aims regarding the fetters, of which giving up is the last."@en owl:sameAs "A statement of purpose: the factors 'should be developed for' (bhāvetabbā) four aims regarding the fetters, of which giving up is the last."@en .

"A sutta's own statement that one term is another. Cited, never merged into one concept."@en owl:sameAs "A sutta's own statement that one term is another. Cited, never merged into one concept."@en .

"A sutta's statement that one quality is twofold, naming the two."@en owl:sameAs "A sutta's statement that one quality is twofold, naming the two."@en .

"A sutta's statement that one thing conditions another."@en owl:sameAs "A sutta's statement that one thing conditions another."@en .

"A sutta's statement that something leads to, or works against, something else."@en owl:sameAs "A sutta's statement that something leads to, or works against, something else."@en .

"All the ascetics and brahmins in the future who will give up the three discriminations will do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "All the ascetics and brahmins in the future who will give up the three discriminations will do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en .

"All the ascetics and brahmins in the present who are giving up the three discriminations do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "All the ascetics and brahmins in the present who are giving up the three discriminations do so by developing and cultivating the seven awakening factors."@en .

"All things are not-self—"@en owl:sameAs "All things are not-self—"@en .

"An image a sutta uses to illustrate a teaching ('seyyathāpi … evameva')."@en owl:sameAs "An image a sutta uses to illustrate a teaching ('seyyathāpi … evameva')."@en .

"And Kuṇḍaliya, how is sense restraint developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the three kinds of good conduct?"@en owl:sameAs "And Kuṇḍaliya, how is sense restraint developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the three kinds of good conduct?"@en .

"And how are the four kinds of mindfulness meditation developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors?"@en owl:sameAs "And how are the four kinds of mindfulness meditation developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the seven awakening factors?"@en .

"And how are the seven awakening factors developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom?"@en owl:sameAs "And how are the seven awakening factors developed and cultivated so as to fulfill knowledge and freedom?"@en .

"And how are the three kinds of good conduct developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation?"@en owl:sameAs "And how are the three kinds of good conduct developed and cultivated so as to fulfill the four kinds of mindfulness meditation?"@en .

"And how is the heart’s release by compassion developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en owl:sameAs "And how is the heart’s release by compassion developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en .

"And how is the heart’s release by equanimity developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en owl:sameAs "And how is the heart’s release by equanimity developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en .

"And how is the heart’s release by love developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en owl:sameAs "And how is the heart’s release by love developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en .

"And how is the heart’s release by rejoicing developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en owl:sameAs "And how is the heart’s release by rejoicing developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en .

"And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity arise, and once they’ve arisen, they’re fully developed.”"@en owl:sameAs "And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity arise, and once they’ve arisen, they’re fully developed.”"@en .

"And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity don’t arise, or if they’ve already arisen, they cease."@en owl:sameAs "And the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity don’t arise, or if they’ve already arisen, they cease."@en .

"And what are the seven awakening factors that are fully developed?"@en owl:sameAs "And what are the seven awakening factors that are fully developed?"@en .

"And what are the seven awakening factors?"@en owl:sameAs "And what are the seven awakening factors?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of doubt, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of restlessness and remorse, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of energy, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of equanimity, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of immersion, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of investigation of principles, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of mindfulness, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of rapture, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en owl:sameAs "And what fuels the arising of the awakening factor of tranquility, or, when it has arisen, fully develops it?"@en .

"And what is the way in which the five hindrances become ten?"@en owl:sameAs "And what is the way in which the five hindrances become ten?"@en .

"And what is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen?"@en owl:sameAs "And what is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen?"@en .

"Any thing at all, as in 'all things are not-self' (sabbe dhammā anattā)."@en owl:sameAs "Any thing at all, as in 'all things are not-self' (sabbe dhammā anattā)."@en .

"Anything the teachings talk about."@en owl:sameAs "Anything the teachings talk about."@en .

"As an attainment: 'the liberation of the beautiful' (subha vimokkha). Not SN 46.51's 'feature of beauty' (subhanimitta), which fuels sensual desire."@en owl:sameAs "As an attainment: 'the liberation of the beautiful' (subha vimokkha). Not SN 46.51's 'feature of beauty' (subhanimitta), which fuels sensual desire."@en .

"As they investigate principles with wisdom in this way their energy is roused up and unflagging."@en owl:sameAs "As they investigate principles with wisdom in this way their energy is roused up and unflagging."@en .

"As they live mindfully in this way they investigate, explore, and inquire into that teaching with wisdom."@en owl:sameAs "As they live mindfully in this way they investigate, explore, and inquire into that teaching with wisdom."@en .

"Aspect"@en owl:sameAs "Aspect"@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of energy; they develop it and perfect it."@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of energy; they develop it and perfect it."@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of equanimity; they develop it and perfect it."@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of equanimity; they develop it and perfect it."@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of immersion; they develop it and perfect it."@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of immersion; they develop it and perfect it."@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of investigation of principles;"@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of investigation of principles;"@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of mindfulness;"@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of mindfulness;"@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of rapture; they develop it and perfect it."@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of rapture; they develop it and perfect it."@en .

"At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of tranquility; they develop it and perfect it."@en owl:sameAs "At such a time, a mendicant has initiated the awakening factor of tranquility; they develop it and perfect it."@en .

