"Equanimity for internal things is the awakening factor of equanimity; and equanimity for external things is also the awakening factor of equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "Equanimity for internal things is the awakening factor of equanimity; and equanimity for external things is also the awakening factor of equanimity."@en .

"Every teaching claim in the text is modelled."@en owl:sameAs "Every teaching claim in the text is modelled."@en .

"Factor of the first jhāna"@en owl:sameAs "Factor of the first jhāna"@en .

"For claims cited by reference only (dho:citationNote): the text referred to, which we do not hold."@en owl:sameAs "For claims cited by reference only (dho:citationNote): the text referred to, which we do not hold."@en .

"Free-text reference for sources we do not hold verbatim (e.g. Visuddhimagga). Claims that only have this are flagged as unverified."@en owl:sameAs "Free-text reference for sources we do not hold verbatim (e.g. Visuddhimagga). Claims that only have this are flagged as unverified."@en .

"Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "Furthermore, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"Hindrance"@en owl:sameAs "Hindrance"@en .

"How many members the text says the list has. SHACL checks the data matches."@en owl:sameAs "How many members the text says the list has. SHACL checks the data matches."@en .

"How the heart's release by compassion is developed (13.1-13.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by compassion."@en owl:sameAs "How the heart's release by compassion is developed (13.1-13.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by compassion."@en .

"How the heart's release by equanimity is developed (15.1-15.3). The Pali even has 'the awakening factor of equanimity accompanied by equanimity' (upekkhāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ, 15.3): the practice and the factor are two things here, which supports keeping them as separate concepts (D15)."@en owl:sameAs "How the heart's release by equanimity is developed (15.1-15.3). The Pali even has 'the awakening factor of equanimity accompanied by equanimity' (upekkhāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ, 15.3): the practice and the factor are two things here, which supports keeping them as separate concepts (D15)."@en .

"How the heart's release by love is developed (12.1-12.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by love. Sujato's English: 'develops the heart's release by love together with the awakening factors'."@en owl:sameAs "How the heart's release by love is developed (12.1-12.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by love. Sujato's English: 'develops the heart's release by love together with the awakening factors'."@en .

"How the heart's release by rejoicing is developed (14.1-14.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by rejoicing."@en owl:sameAs "How the heart's release by rejoicing is developed (14.1-14.3). The Pali: each awakening factor developed accompanied by rejoicing."@en .

"If not, they attain enlightenment at the time of death."@en owl:sameAs "If not, they attain enlightenment at the time of death."@en .

"If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they head upstream, going to the Akaniṭṭha realm."@en owl:sameAs "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they head upstream, going to the Akaniṭṭha realm."@en .

"If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished upon landing."@en owl:sameAs "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished upon landing."@en .

"If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished with extra effort."@en owl:sameAs "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished with extra effort."@en .

"If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished without extra effort."@en owl:sameAs "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters they’re extinguished without extra effort."@en .

"If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters, they’re extinguished between one life and the next."@en owl:sameAs "If not, with the ending of the five lower fetters, they’re extinguished between one life and the next."@en .

"If they wish: ‘May I meditate staying equanimous, mindful and aware, shunning both the repulsive and the unrepulsive,’ that’s what they do."@en owl:sameAs "If they wish: ‘May I meditate staying equanimous, mindful and aware, shunning both the repulsive and the unrepulsive,’ that’s what they do."@en .

"Ill will for what is internal is a hindrance; and ill will for what is external is also a hindrance."@en owl:sameAs "Ill will for what is internal is a hindrance; and ill will for what is external is also a hindrance."@en .

"Immersion while placing the mind and keeping it connected is the awakening factor of immersion; and immersion without placing the mind and keeping it connected is also the awakening factor of immersion."@en owl:sameAs "Immersion while placing the mind and keeping it connected is the awakening factor of immersion; and immersion without placing the mind and keeping it connected is also the awakening factor of immersion."@en .

"In SN 46.33:2.3 the Pali names only sensual desire and abbreviates the rest (…pe…); the other four members are the conventional expansion, as the translation gives them."@en owl:sameAs "In SN 46.33:2.3 the Pali names only sensual desire and abbreviates the rest (…pe…); the other four members are the conventional expansion, as the translation gives them."@en .

"In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en .

"In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en .

"In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en .

"In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en .

"In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue."@en .

"In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue.”"@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, the seven awakening factors are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue.”"@en .

"In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en .

"In the same way, there’s a time when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt and you don’t truly understand the escape from doubt that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both. Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, there’s a time when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt and you don’t truly understand the escape from doubt that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both. Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en .

"In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of equanimity’ becomes twofold."@en owl:sameAs "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of equanimity’ becomes twofold."@en .

"In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of immersion’ becomes twofold."@en owl:sameAs "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of immersion’ becomes twofold."@en .

"In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of rapture’ becomes twofold."@en owl:sameAs "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of rapture’ becomes twofold."@en .

"In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of tranquility’ becomes twofold."@en owl:sameAs "In this way what is concisely referred to as ‘the awakening factor of tranquility’ becomes twofold."@en .

"Investigating, exploring, and inquiring into internal things with wisdom is the awakening factor of investigation of principles; and investigating, exploring, and inquiring into external things with wisdom is also the awakening factor of investigation of principles."@en owl:sameAs "Investigating, exploring, and inquiring into internal things with wisdom is the awakening factor of investigation of principles; and investigating, exploring, and inquiring into external things with wisdom is also the awakening factor of investigation of principles."@en .

"Iron,"@en owl:sameAs "Iron,"@en .

"Iron, copper, tin, lead and silver are the five corruptions of gold (1.3-1.7); the point names five corruptions of the mind (cittassa upakkilesā, 2.1), not 'hindrances'."@en owl:sameAs "Iron, copper, tin, lead and silver are the five corruptions of gold (1.3-1.7); the point names five corruptions of the mind (cittassa upakkilesā, 2.1), not 'hindrances'."@en .

"It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en owl:sameAs "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en .

"It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by compassion together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en owl:sameAs "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by compassion together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en .

