"Pali"@en owl:sameAs "Pali"@en .

"Pali: 'these seven awakening factors, developed and cultivated, arise unarisen, not apart from (nāññatra) the appearance of a Realized One'. 'To be developed and cultivated' is Sujato's reading of bhāvitā bahulīkatā. A necessary condition, not a sufficient one (D23)."@en owl:sameAs "Pali: 'these seven awakening factors, developed and cultivated, arise unarisen, not apart from (nāññatra) the appearance of a Realized One'. 'To be developed and cultivated' is Sujato's reading of bhāvitā bahulīkatā. A necessary condition, not a sufficient one (D23)."@en .

"Passage"@en owl:sameAs "Passage"@en .

"Physical energy is the awakening factor of energy; and mental energy is also the awakening factor of energy."@en owl:sameAs "Physical energy is the awakening factor of energy; and mental energy is also the awakening factor of energy."@en .

"Physical tranquility is the awakening factor of tranquility; and mental tranquility is also the awakening factor of tranquility."@en owl:sameAs "Physical tranquility is the awakening factor of tranquility; and mental tranquility is also the awakening factor of tranquility."@en .

"Placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en owl:sameAs "Placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en .

"Plain description of what in this text is NOT modelled, so nobody mistakes partial for complete."@en owl:sameAs "Plain description of what in this text is NOT modelled, so nobody mistakes partial for complete."@en .

"Plain description of what was modelled from this text."@en owl:sameAs "Plain description of what was modelled from this text."@en .

