    dho:segment "mn43:20.3" ;
    dho:textEn "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idhāvuso, paṭhamaṁ jhānaṁ samāpannassa bhikkhuno kāmacchando pahīno hoti, byāpādo pahīno hoti, thinamiddhaṁ pahīnaṁ hoti, uddhaccakukkuccaṁ pahīnaṁ hoti, vicikicchā pahīnā hoti;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato#mn43:20.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.1-1.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.1-1.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.1 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.1:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sīlaṁ nissāya sīle patiṭṭhāya satta bojjhaṅge bhāvento satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaronto mahantattaṁ vepullattaṁ pāpuṇāti dhammesu."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato#sn46.1:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.10-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.10-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.10 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.10:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, these seven awakening factors don’t arise to be developed and cultivated apart from the Holy One’s training."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā anuppannā uppajjanti, nāññatra sugatavinayā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.10/en/sujato#sn46.10:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.11-1.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.11-1.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.11 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.11:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu sīlaṁ nissāya sīle patiṭṭhāya satta bojjhaṅge bhāveti, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaroti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.11/en/sujato#sn46.11:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.12-1.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.12-1.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.12 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.12:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ nimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—kalyāṇamittatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.12/en/sujato#sn46.12:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.13-1.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.13-1.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.13 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.13:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—yonisomanasikāro."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.13/en/sujato#sn46.13:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.9 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.130-1.9 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.9" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which culminate in the removal of greed, hate, and delusion. …”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti rāgavinayapariyosānaṁ dosavinayapariyosānaṁ mohavinayapariyosānaṁ …"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.9"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-1.5 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.24-1.5 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:1.5" ;
    dho:textEn "and doubt arise, and once arisen they increase and grow."@en ;
    dho:textPi "anuppannā ceva vicikicchā uppajjati, uppannā ca vicikicchā bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:1.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.24-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.24-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.24 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.24:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When you apply the mind rationally, sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yoniso ca kho, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando nuppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando pahīyati;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.24/en/sujato#sn46.24:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.3-9.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way they can expect seven fruits and benefits."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitesu kho, bhikkhave, sattasu sambojjhaṅgesu evaṁ bahulīkatesu satta phalā sattānisaṁsā pāṭikaṅkhā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.3-9.10 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.3-9.10 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.3 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.3:9.10" ;
    dho:textEn "When the seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated in this way these are the seven fruits and benefits they can expect.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitesu kho, bhikkhave, sattasu bojjhaṅgesu evaṁ bahulīkatesu ime satta phalā sattānisaṁsā pāṭikaṅkhā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.3/en/sujato#sn46.3:9.10"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.33-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.33-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.33 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.33:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, bhikkhave, pañcime cittassa upakkilesā, yehi upakkilesehi upakkiliṭṭhaṁ cittaṁ na ceva mudu hoti na ca kammaniyaṁ, na ca pabhassaraṁ pabhaṅgu ca, na ca sammā samādhiyati āsavānaṁ khayāya."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.33/en/sujato#sn46.33:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.35-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.35-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.35 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.35:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, when you apply the mind irrationally, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt arise, and once arisen they increase and grow.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Ayoniso, bhikkhave, manasikaroto anuppanno ceva kāmacchando uppajjati, uppanno ca kāmacchando bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppanno ceva byāpādo uppajjati, uppanno ca byāpādo bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannañceva thinamiddhaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca thinamiddhaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannañceva uddhaccakukkuccaṁ uppajjati, uppannañca uddhaccakukkuccaṁ bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattati; anuppannā ceva vicikicchā uppajjati, uppannā ca vicikicchā bhiyyobhāvāya vepullāya saṁvattatī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.35/en/sujato#sn46.35:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.37-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, there are these five obstacles and hindrances, corruptions of the heart that weaken wisdom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcime, bhikkhave, āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso upakkilesā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.37-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.37-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.37 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.37:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "There are these seven awakening factors that are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.37/en/sujato#sn46.37:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.38-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye ariyasāvako aṭṭhiṁ katvā manasi katvā sabbaṁ cetaso samannāharitvā ohitasoto dhammaṁ suṇāti, imassa pañca nīvaraṇā tasmiṁ samaye na honti. Satta bojjhaṅgā tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.38-3.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.38-3.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.38 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.38:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "Sometimes a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly, and actively listens to the teaching. At such a time the five hindrances are absent, and the seven awakening factors are fully developed.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Yasmiṁ, bhikkhave, samaye ariyasāvako aṭṭhiṁ katvā manasi katvā sabbaṁ cetaso samannāharitvā ohitasoto dhammaṁ suṇāti, imassa pañca nīvaraṇā tasmiṁ samaye na honti. Ime satta bojjhaṅgā tasmiṁ samaye bhāvanāpāripūriṁ gacchantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.38/en/sujato#sn46.38:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "There are these five obstacles and hindrances, parasites of the mind that weaken wisdom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Pañcime, bhikkhave, āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso ajjhāruhā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.3" ;
    dho:textEn "Sensual desire,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kāmacchando, bhikkhave, āvaraṇo nīvaraṇo cetaso ajjhāruho paññāya dubbalīkaraṇo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "ill will,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Byāpādo, bhikkhave, āvaraṇo nīvaraṇo cetaso ajjhāruho paññāya dubbalīkaraṇo."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.5 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.5 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.5" ;
    dho:textEn "dullness and drowsiness,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Thinamiddhaṁ, bhikkhave, āvaraṇaṁ nīvaraṇaṁ cetaso ajjhāruhaṁ paññāya dubbalīkaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.6 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.6 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "restlessness and remorse,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Uddhaccakukkuccaṁ, bhikkhave, āvaraṇaṁ nīvaraṇaṁ cetaso ajjhāruhaṁ paññāya dubbalīkaraṇaṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-2.7 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-2.7 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:2.7" ;
    dho:textEn "and doubt."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Vicikicchā, bhikkhave, āvaraṇā nīvaraṇā cetaso ajjhāruhā paññāya dubbalīkaraṇā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:2.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-3.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-3.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:3.1" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or parasites of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anajjhāruhā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:3.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.39-3.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.39-3.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.39 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.39:3.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anajjhāruho bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo, bhikkhave, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anajjhāruho bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.39/en/sujato#sn46.39:3.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-1.8 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.40-1.8 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "These five hindrances are destroyers of sight, vision, and knowledge. They block wisdom, they’re on the side of distress, and they don’t lead to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, pañca nīvaraṇā andhakaraṇā acakkhukaraṇā aññāṇakaraṇā paññānirodhikā vighātapakkhiyā anibbānasaṁvattanikā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.40-2.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.40-2.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.40 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.40:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are creators of vision and knowledge. They grow wisdom, they’re on the side of solace, and they lead to extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā cakkhukaraṇā ñāṇakaraṇā paññābuddhiyā avighātapakkhiyā nibbānasaṁvattanikā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.40/en/sujato#sn46.40:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.48-1.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.48-1.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.48 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.48:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, for a mendicant good friendship is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno sattannaṁ bojjhaṅgānaṁ uppādāya etaṁ pubbaṅgamaṁ etaṁ pubbanimittaṁ, yadidaṁ—kalyāṇamittatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.48/en/sujato#sn46.48:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-1.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.51-1.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, I will teach you what fuels and what starves the five hindrances and the seven awakening factors."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Pañcannañca, bhikkhave, nīvaraṇānaṁ sattannañca bojjhaṅgānaṁ āhārañca anāhārañca desessāmi;"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.51-7.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.51-7.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.51 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.51:7.2" ;
    dho:senseAssignedBy "editor; matches Sujato's rendering 'qualities'" ;
    dho:textEn "There are qualities that are skillful and unskillful, blameworthy and blameless, inferior and superior, and those with a portion of dark or bright."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.51/en/sujato#sn46.51:7.2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    dho:usesSense dho:sense-dhamma-quality .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.54-12.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by love developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, mettācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.54-13.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by compassion developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, karuṇācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.54-14.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by rejoicing developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, muditācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.54-15.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And how is the heart’s release by equanimity developed? What is its destination, apex, fruit, and end?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Kathaṁ bhāvitā ca, bhikkhave, upekkhācetovimutti, kiṅgatikā hoti, kiṁparamā, kiṁphalā, kiṁpariyosānā?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-10.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-10.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:10.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in restlessness and remorse … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, brāhmaṇa, yasmiṁ samaye uddhaccakukkuccapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati uddhaccakukkuccaparetena, uppannassa ca uddhaccakukkuccassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati, paratthampi …pe… ubhayatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati; dīgharattaṁ sajjhāyakatāpi mantā nappaṭibhanti, pageva asajjhāyakatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:10.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-12.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-12.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:12.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, there’s a time when your heart is overcome and mired in doubt and you don’t truly understand the escape from doubt that has arisen. At that time you don’t truly know or see what is good for yourself, good for another, or good for both. Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, brāhmaṇa, yasmiṁ samaye vicikicchāpariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati vicikicchāparetena, uppannāya ca vicikicchāya nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati, paratthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati, ubhayatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati; dīgharattaṁ sajjhāyakatāpi mantā nappaṭibhanti, pageva asajjhāyakatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:12.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-23.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-23.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:23.1" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Sattime, brāhmaṇa, bojjhaṅgā anāvaraṇā anīvaraṇā cetaso anupakkilesā bhāvitā bahulīkatā vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:23.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-23.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-23.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:23.3" ;
    dho:textEn "The awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Satisambojjhaṅgo kho, brāhmaṇa, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo kho, brāhmaṇa, anāvaraṇo anīvaraṇo cetaso anupakkileso bhāvito bahulīkato vijjāvimuttiphalasacchikiriyāya saṁvattati."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:23.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-4.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-4.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:4.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, brāhmaṇa, yasmiṁ samaye kāmarāgapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati kāmarāgaparetena, uppannassa ca kāmarāgassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati …pe… paratthampi …pe… ubhayatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati; dīgharattaṁ sajjhāyakatāpi mantā nappaṭibhanti, pageva asajjhāyakatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:4.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-6.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-6.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:6.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in ill will … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, brāhmaṇa, yasmiṁ samaye byāpādapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati byāpādaparetena, uppannassa ca byāpādassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati, paratthampi tasmiṁ samaye …pe… ubhayatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati; dīgharattaṁ sajjhāyakatāpi mantā nappaṭibhanti, pageva asajjhāyakatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:6.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.55-8.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.55-8.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.55 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.55:8.3" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, when your heart is overcome and mired in dullness and drowsiness … Even hymns that are long-rehearsed don’t spring to mind, let alone those that are not rehearsed."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evameva kho, brāhmaṇa, yasmiṁ samaye thinamiddhapariyuṭṭhitena cetasā viharati thinamiddhaparetena, uppannassa ca thinamiddhassa nissaraṇaṁ yathābhūtaṁ nappajānāti, attatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati, paratthampi …pe… ubhayatthampi tasmiṁ samaye yathābhūtaṁ na jānāti na passati; dīgharattaṁ sajjhāyakatāpi mantā nappaṭibhanti, pageva asajjhāyakatā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.55/en/sujato#sn46.55:8.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-1.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-1.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of a skeleton together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“When the perception of a skeleton is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results: enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Aṭṭhikasaññāya, bhikkhave, bhāvitāya bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-2.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-2.5 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-2.5 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:2.5" ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitāya kho, bhikkhave, aṭṭhikasaññāya evaṁ bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:2.5"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-3.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-3.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:3.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-4.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-4.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:4.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:4.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-5.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-5.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:5.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:5.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.57-6.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.57-6.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.57 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.57:6.4" ;
    dho:textPi "aṭṭhikasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.57/en/sujato#sn46.57:6.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.6-2.4 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.4" ;
    dho:textEn "“The four kinds of mindfulness meditation.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Cattāro kho, kuṇḍaliya, satipaṭṭhānā bhāvitā bahulīkatā satta bojjhaṅge paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.6-2.6 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.6-2.6 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.6 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.6:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "“The three kinds of good conduct.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Tīṇi kho, kuṇḍaliya, sucaritāni bhāvitāni bahulīkatāni cattāro satipaṭṭhāne paripūrentī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.6/en/sujato#sn46.6:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.7-1.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.7-1.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.7 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.7:1.2" ;
    dho:textEn "In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "evameva kho, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satta bojjhaṅge bhāvento satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkaronto nibbānaninno hoti nibbānapoṇo nibbānapabbhāro."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato#sn46.7:1.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-1.3 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-1.3 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:1.3" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:1.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-2.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.1" ;
    dho:textEn "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated you can expect one of two results:"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Nirodhasaññāya, bhikkhave, bhāvitāya bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.2 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-2.2 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.2" ;
    dho:textEn "enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return."@en ;
    dho:textPi "diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitā."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.7 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-2.7 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.7" ;
    dho:textEn "When the perception of cessation is developed and cultivated in this way you can expect one of two results:"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Evaṁ bhāvitāya kho, bhikkhave, nirodhasaññāya evaṁ bahulīkatāya dvinnaṁ phalānaṁ aññataraṁ phalaṁ pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.8 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.76-2.8 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.8" ;
    dho:textEn "enlightenment in this very life, or if there’s residue left behind, non-return.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "diṭṭheva dhamme aññā, sati vā upādisese anāgāmitāti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.9-1.1 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Passage ;
    owl:sameAs dho:p-sn46.9-1.1 ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.9 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.9:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, these seven awakening factors don’t arise to be developed and cultivated except when a Realized One, a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha has appeared."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā anuppannā uppajjanti, nāññatra tathāgatassa pātubhāvā arahato sammāsambuddhassa."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.9/en/sujato#sn46.9:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

