    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.10 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.10 Dutiyauppannasutta — Arisen (2nd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The list (1.1, 1.3), and the teaching: the seven awakening factors, unarisen, don't arise apart from the Holy One's training (1.1, 1.4; D23). The chapter's summary verse (2.0-2.4) lists the chapter's titles and is not teaching." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-16"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.10/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.14 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.14 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.14 Paṭhamagilānasutta — Sick (1st)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The Buddha to the sick Mahākassapa: the seven awakening factors, rightly explained, developed and cultivated, lead to direct knowledge, awakening and extinguishment (3.1-3.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting and the exchange about his pain (1.1-2.2). Mahākassapa's affirmation (3.5-3.6). The narrative that he recovered from the illness (4.1-4.4): narrated, not taught. The Pali links the recovery to the episode, 'in that way that illness was abandoned' (tathāpahīno, 4.4, untranslated), but it teaches nothing about the factors curing illness." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.14/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.15 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.15 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.15 Dutiyagilānasutta — Sick (2nd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The Buddha to the sick Mahāmoggallāna: the same statement as SN 46.14 (3.1-3.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting and the exchange about his pain (1.1-2.2). Moggallāna's affirmation (3.5-3.6). The narrative of his recovery (4.1-4.4, with the Pali-only 'in that way that illness was abandoned', 4.4): narrated, not taught." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.15/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.17 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.17 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.17 Pāraṅgamasutta — Going to the Far Shore"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to going from the near shore to the far shore (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The verses (2.1-6.6): few cross to the far shore, the astute develop the bright, and those rightly developed in the awakening factors are quenched in this world." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.17/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.19 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.19 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.19 Ariyasutta — Noble"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors brings one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are 'noble and emancipating' (ariyā niyyānikā) (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.19/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.20 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.20 Nibbidāsutta — Disillusionment"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening (sambodhi) and extinguishment (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.22 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.22 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.22 Bojjhaṅgadesanāsutta — A Teaching on the Awakening Factors"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Its whole teaching: the list of the seven awakening factors (1.1, 1.3, 1.4), as citations on the existing list." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.22/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.31 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.31 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.31 Paṭhamakusalasutta — Skillful (1st)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in diligence (1.1); a diligent mendicant can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "'Diligence is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.31/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.32 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.32 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.32 Dutiyakusalasutta — Skillful (2nd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "'Rational application of mind is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.32/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.34 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.34 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.34 Anupakkilesasutta — Not Corruptions"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are not obstacles, hindrances or corruptions of the mind (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.34/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.36 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.36 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.36 Buddhisutta — Growth"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to growth and progress (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.36/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.4 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.4 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.4 Vatthasutta — Clothes"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Sāriputta names the seven awakening factors (2.1-2.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "Sāriputta's account of his own practice: he meditates in whichever factor he wishes, morning, midday and evening; knows each as limitless and properly implemented; understands that it remains while it remains, and the reason when it subsides (2.5-2.11, repeated 3.5-3.11). The simile of a chest of garments (3.1-3.4). No pattern yet for a practitioner's account or for similes." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.4/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.8 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.8 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.8 Upavānasutta — With Upavāṇa"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Taught by Venerable Upavāṇa to Sāriputta: the seven awakening factors, properly implemented by rational application of mind, lead to living at ease (2.1-2.2, 3.3)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting (1.1-1.3). What a mendicant understands as they rouse up each factor: 'my mind is well freed, dullness and drowsiness eradicated, restlessness and remorse eliminated, energy roused up, mind sharply focused, not sluggish' (3.1-3.2). No pattern yet for what is known in practice; read as outcomes it would overstate the text." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.8/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.9 a owl:Thing,
        dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    owl:sameAs dho:t-sn46.9 ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.9 Paṭhamauppannasutta — Arisen (1st)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The list (1.1, 1.3), and the teaching: the seven awakening factors, unarisen, don't arise apart from the appearance of a Realized One (1.1, 1.4; D23)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-16"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.9/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

"When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment" owl:sameAs "When developed and cultivated, they lead to direct knowledge, to awakening, and to extinguishment" .

"can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors" owl:sameAs "can expect to develop and cultivate the seven awakening factors" .

"on seclusion, fading away, and cessation" owl:sameAs "on seclusion, fading away, and cessation" .

"A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en owl:sameAs "A mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en .

"Frequent irrational application of mind to them"@en owl:sameAs "Frequent irrational application of mind to them"@en .

"It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en owl:sameAs "It’s when a mendicant develops the perception of cessation together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en .

"Sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt."@en owl:sameAs "Sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt."@en .

"There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of equanimity."@en .

"There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en owl:sameAs "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of mindfulness."@en .

"There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of rapture."@en owl:sameAs "There are things that are grounds for the awakening factor of rapture."@en .

"There are things that are the basis of serenity and freedom from distraction."@en owl:sameAs "There are things that are the basis of serenity and freedom from distraction."@en .

"There is tranquility of the body and of the mind."@en owl:sameAs "There is tranquility of the body and of the mind."@en .

"These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en owl:sameAs "These seven awakening factors are not obstacles, hindrances, or corruptions of the mind. When developed and cultivated they lead to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom.”"@en .

"This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en owl:sameAs "This body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue."@en .

"dullness and drowsiness,"@en owl:sameAs "dullness and drowsiness,"@en .

"ill will,"@en owl:sameAs "ill will,"@en .

"restlessness and remorse,"@en owl:sameAs "restlessness and remorse,"@en .

"“Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise."@en owl:sameAs "“Mendicants, the dawn is the forerunner and harbinger of the sunrise."@en .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, kusalākusalā dhammā sāvajjānavajjā dhammā hīnapaṇītā dhammā kaṇhasukkasappaṭibhāgā dhammā."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, pītisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, pītisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, samathanimittaṁ abyagganimittaṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, samathanimittaṁ abyagganimittaṁ."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, satisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, satisambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi .

"Atthi, bhikkhave, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi owl:sameAs "Atthi, bhikkhave, upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṭṭhānīyā dhammā."@pi .

"Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi owl:sameAs "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti …pe…"@pi .

"Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi owl:sameAs "Kalyāṇamittassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi .

"Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi owl:sameAs "Satisambojjhaṅgo …pe… upekkhāsambojjhaṅgo."@pi .

"Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi owl:sameAs "Seyyathāpi, bhikkhave, ayaṁ kāyo āhāraṭṭhitiko, āhāraṁ paṭicca tiṭṭhati, anāhāro no tiṭṭhati;"@pi .

"Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi owl:sameAs "Yonisomanasikārasampannassetaṁ, bhikkhave, bhikkhuno pāṭikaṅkhaṁ—satta bojjhaṅge bhāvessati, satta bojjhaṅge bahulīkarissati."@pi .

"nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi owl:sameAs "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi .

